There are different ways to terminate a C program:

1. Using the return statement: You can use the return statement to terminate a program immediately. This can be used in functions to return a value to the calling function and exit the function.

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello World\n");
    return 0;
}
```

2. Using the exit() function: The exit() function is used to terminate the program immediately. It takes an integer status code as an argument, which represents the exit status of the program.

```c
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello World\n");
    exit(0);
}
```

3. Using the return 0; statement outside of a function: If you want to terminate the program immediately after the main() function, you can use the return 0; statement outside of the function.

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello World\n");
    // return 0;

